<article class="env-corollary" id="82D0B0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/82D0B0">Corollary <span data-tag="82D0B0">6.5.3.13</span> <span class="named">(Dugger-Hollander-Isaksen <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/hollander">hollander</a>]</span>, Toën-Vezzosi <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/toen">toen</a>]</span>)</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be an $\infty $-topos. For each $X \in \calX $ and each hypercovering $U_{\bullet }$ of $\calX _{/X}$, let $|U_{\bullet }|$ be the associated morphism of $\calX $ $($which has target $X$$)$. Let $S$ denote the collection of all such morphisms $|U_{\bullet }|$. Then $\calX ^{\wedge } = S^{-1} \calX $. In other words, an object of $\calX $ is hypercomplete if and only if it is $S$-local. </p>
